# TradeKaro

A full-stack MERN trading platform simulator — built end-to-end to understand how modern discount brokerages actually work under the hood: order flow, live market data, portfolio tracking, authentication, and support systems.

**Live demo:** [https://trade-karo-nine.vercel.app](https://trade-karo-nine.vercel.app/)

---

## Why this project

Most trading platform tutorials stop at a static UI. TradeKaro is a **working system** — every screen, from signup to order placement, is backed by a real REST API and a real database. There's no mock data and no shortcuts. The goal wasn't to copy an existing product but to understand how modern discount brokerages work: figuring out the small UX and architecture decisions that make a trading interface feel trustworthy, and implementing them from scratch.

---

## Features

### Authentication

- JWT-based signup/login with bcrypt password hashing
- Cross-app token handoff (separate landing/marketing app and dashboard app, connected via a shared auth flow)
- Session verification on load (`/verify`) with automatic logout on expired/invalid tokens
- Protected routes on both frontend and backend

### Live Market Data

- Real stock data (S&P 500 symbols) sourced from Finnhub
- In-memory caching layer to minimize external API calls and avoid unnecessary load, keyed per symbol with a short TTL
- **WebSocket-based real-time price streaming** (Socket.io) — prices push to connected clients instead of polling, with an immediate one-time quote sent on subscribe so the UI doesn't wait for the next broadcast tick
- Searchable stock discovery — add any of the tracked symbols to a personal watchlist

### Trading

- Buy/Sell order placement with **CNC (delivery)** and **MIS (intraday)** product types
- Server-side validation before any state mutation (insufficient funds, invalid sell quantity, no holding/position to sell) — validate-first, mutate-later pattern to avoid partial/inconsistent writes
- Weighted-average cost calculation on repeated buys
- Virtual wallet (Funds) — balance deducted on buy, credited on sell, with an order-level insufficient-funds check

### Portfolio Tracking

- **Holdings** (CNC positions) with live P&L, day change %, and a portfolio-allocation donut chart
- **Positions** (MIS/intraday) with live P&L, separate from delivery holdings
- **Orders** — full order history log, sorted latest-first, per user
- **Dashboard** — consolidated view of equity, holdings P&L, and open intraday positions

### Analytics

- MongoDB aggregation pipelines for trading insights: total trades, most-traded stock, buy/sell breakdown
- Monthly trade volume trend, visualized as a line chart

### Support

- Built-in ticketing-style support center on the marketing site
- Functional contact form — messages delivered via a real SMTP email pipeline (Nodemailer + Gmail App Password), with `replyTo` wired to the sender so replies go straight back to them

### UI/UX Design System

- **Custom design tokens**: a 4-color brand palette (`brand-dark`, `brand-mid`, `brand-light`, `brand-pale`) defined via Tailwind v4's `@theme`, applied consistently across the landing pages and the trading dashboard — including buy/sell semantic colors, live-data pulse indicators, and chart theming
- **Typography system**: Space Grotesk for headings, Inter for body text, applied uniformly through custom `font-heading` / `font-body` utility classes
- **Live-data visual language**: reusable "live" motifs (pulsing status dots, animated SVG price charts, real-time WebSocket-driven watchlist) used across the marketing site and dashboard to visually reinforce the platform's real-time nature
- **Responsive, mobile-first layouts**: every page — including the trading dashboard, modals, and navigation — is built with distinct mobile / tablet / desktop breakpoints, using stacked card views on mobile and full data tables on larger screens
- **Accessible interaction patterns**: modals use React portals to escape parent stacking contexts, include body-scroll locking while open, and support click-outside-to-close; navigation menus support keyboard focus states and screen-reader labels
- **Consistent component library**: shared UI primitives (buttons, cards, badges, form inputs) follow a single visual language (rounded-2xl cards, branded shadows, ring-based focus states) across both the public site and the authenticated dashboard

---

## Tech Stack

**Frontend**

- React + Vite
- Tailwind CSS v4 (custom design tokens via `@theme`)
- Chart.js (portfolio allocation, watchlist trend, analytics)
- Socket.io-client (real-time price streaming)
- React Router

**Backend**

- Node.js + Express (MVC-style structure — routes → controllers → services)
- MongoDB + Mongoose
- Socket.io (WebSocket server)
- JWT + bcryptjs (auth)
- Nodemailer (contact form email delivery)
- Finnhub API — live market data source

---

## Architecture Notes

- **Two frontend apps**: a public marketing/landing site and an authenticated trading dashboard, connected by a JWT handoff over a redirect URL — mirroring how real brokerages separate their marketing site from their trading platform
- **Live data, not stored data**: prices are never persisted to the database — only a short-lived in-memory cache. Only user actions (orders, holdings, positions, funds) are stored
- **WebSocket subscription model**: clients emit `subscribe` with their watchlist symbols; the server tracks a global `Set` of subscribed symbols (deduplicated across users) and broadcasts on a fixed interval, plus an immediate quote on first subscribe for fast initial load
- **MVC separation** for newer features (contact form, notifications) — routes handle only path→controller mapping, controllers handle request validation and response shaping, services hold the actual business logic (e.g., email sending, price broadcasting) independent of Express's `req`/`res`

---

## Project Structure

```
TRADEKARO/
├── backend/
│   ├── controllers/       # Request handling logic
│   ├── middleware/         # JWT verification
│   ├── model/               # Mongoose schemas
│   ├── routes/               # Express route definitions
│   ├── services/             # Business logic (email, stock data, price broadcasting)
│   ├── sockets/               # Socket.io connection handlers
│   ├── data/                   # Static stock symbol list
│   └── index.js
├── dashboard/                   # Trading dashboard (authenticated app)
│   └── src/
│       ├── components/
│       ├── context/               # AuthContext
│       └── utils/                  # axios instance, socket client
└── frontend/                       # Public marketing/landing site
    └── src/
        └── landing_page/
```

